## 6. Whose point of view decides the sound

Each mode needs a clear "point-of-view side". Put that logic in **one** helper (for example `audioPerspective(battle)`) and cover it with tests.

| Mode | Opponent / Player ejection | Post-match music |
|---|---|---|
| **Quick Battle** (Regular and Custom) | Player 1's fighter is the player; the CPU is the opponent | Victory if Player 1 wins, Defeat if Player 1 loses |
| **Online Play** | This device's player is the player | From this player's side, as the result is already shown |
| **Local Play** | **Universal ejection** for both, always | **Always Victory**, whoever wins, to avoid confusion |
| **Watch Mode** (CPU vs CPU, nobody is the protagonist) | **Universal ejection** | **Victory** (the same reasoning as Local Play) |
| **Practice Ground** | The player's fighter is the player; the dummy is the opponent | No music, only ambience |
| **Any draw** (no winner, nobody ejected), in every mode, Local and Watch included | — | That stage's own **Draw** version |

